# The committed BPF object embeds BTF line information, which contains the
# source lines verbatim - including a trailing CR if the checkout has CRLF
# endings. A CRLF checkout therefore regenerates a byte-different object and
# breaks the CI regenerate-and-diff check of ADR-S1a-05. Pin LF here so the
# object is reproducible from a Windows checkout as well as a Linux one.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.o binary
